                <pb facs="0725" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg717"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.00/743: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-03T17:00:00+09:00">June 3, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 3—7:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>145. My telegram No. 144, June 1, 10 p.m. We have just learned by telephone from
                    the Foreign Office that Hirota has accepted the Foreign Affairs portfolio. The
                    reappointment of Ministers of War and of the Navy has been confirmed. Kaya, now
                    Vice Minister of Finance, has accepted the Ministry of Finance.</p>
                <p>It is generally expected that the formation of the new Cabinet will be completed
                    before end of the day.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
